# VoxCPM2 TTS server (cloned voice + per-utterance style notes) — JUPITER, on one of its two RTX 5080s.
#
# The live voice once the move is done (Jupiter .env: TTS_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8004). It
# moved off Helios GPU1 so the brain can run its native 262144 context (header of
# tts/llama-server-primary.service). Same server and API as before (tts/voxcpm_server.py); only the
# box changed. tts/voxcpm-tts.service is the Helios copy, kept installed but DISABLED as rollback.
#
# Why Jupiter: it is always on, and since 2026-11-21 it holds two RTX 5080s (16 GB, Blackwell sm_120).
# The first target, Saturn's RTX 3090, passed every check but speed: 1.75-2.1x Helios, GPU-bound
# (99-100 % busy at ~1.7 GHz). Saturn stays as the backup box. Measured on the Jupiter 5080 (runbook
# step 2, docs/VOICE_AND_TTS.md → VoxCPM2 on Jupiter): see the table there.
#
# Which card: the two 5080s are identical, so the voice card is picked by UUID, never by index or
# name, in /etc/voxcpm-tts.env (step 5). The other card is for experiments and other models. The same
# UUID goes in Jupiter's .env as JUPITER_TTS_GPU_UUID: Prometheus labels that card gpu_role="tts",
# which TTSGPUMemoryLow selects (the cards can't be told apart by name). Change both together. A
# missing or wrong .env value fires TTSGPUUnmonitored instead of silently disabling the alert.
# Memory: VoxCPM2 takes ~7.4 GiB fresh and grew to 9.3-9.7 GiB on Helios with ordinary texts (PyTorch
# keeps its peak cached and voxcpm never releases it; the VAE decodes a whole clip at once in fp32).
# The install test caps it at 14 GiB of the card's 15.9.
# Don't add PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments to save memory: VoxCPM2 compiles with
# mode="reduce-overhead" (CUDA graphs), and the two were never tested together.
#
# Experiments MUST be pinned to the other card, by UUID: llama.cpp auto-fit and most tools use every
# GPU they can see, and single-GPU tools take cuda:0. Put the voice on the card with the HIGHER PCI bus
# number, so cuda:0 (CUDA orders identical cards by bus) is the experiment card, and pin anyway:
#   export CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID
#   export CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=GPU-<experiment card uuid>
# Docker containers need nvidia-container-toolkit (not installed on Jupiter) and then
# `--gpus device=GPU-<experiment card uuid>`. Jupiter runs all of production (HA, the orchestrator,
# monitoring): an experiment also competes for its RAM and CPU, so keep them small, publish them on
# 127.0.0.1 only, and stop them when done. TTSGPUMemoryLow (quiet) catches an experiment on the voice
# card; one under ~4 GiB only shows as slower speech.
#
# Driver: NVIDIA's open kernel module (nvidia-580-open, prebuilt linux-modules-nvidia-580-open-*).
# Kernel updates have dropped it on all three boxes: unattended-upgrades installs a security kernel but
# keeps the NVIDIA packages back whenever upgrading them means removing an old module package, so the
# next reboot comes up with no driver. NvidiaModuleMissing (quiet) warns BEFORE that reboot (host
# check scripts/check_nvidia_modules.py, textfile metric): fix with `sudo apt full-upgrade`, which moves
# the kernel and its NVIDIA modules together. JupiterGpuDriverBroken (quiet) fires after the fact
# (nvidia-smi failing). The server refuses to run on CPU (VOXCPM_REQUIRE_CUDA), so a lost driver shows
# up as TTSDown, not as a ~7 s/sentence voice.
#
# Network: systemd listens for it (tts/voxcpm-tts-jupiter.socket, socket activation) on 172.17.0.1:8004,
# Docker's default-bridge gateway, which is what host-gateway (host.docker.internal) resolves to inside
# containers. The socket admits only Docker's address pools, so containers reach it and nothing on the
# LAN or the tailnet does; this service itself runs with IPAddressDeny=any, so the server can't open
# connections of its own (to other containers' internal ports, say). It speaks in a cloned voice, and
# Cast speakers play audio from any LAN host, so a caller that can synthesize can make Jess "say" things
# on the house speakers. Hence the bearer key: every path but /health needs
# `Authorization: Bearer <key>` from /etc/voxcpm-tts/api-key (step 5b); Jupiter's .env carries the same
# value as TTS_API_KEY, which the orchestrator sends only to TTS_URL's origin (orchestrator/model_auth.py).
# NEVER listen on 0.0.0.0 or the LAN address, and never add the LAN or the tailnet to the socket's
# allow-list. If Docker's bridge address ever changes ("bip" in /etc/docker/daemon.json), change
# ListenStream in the socket unit to match `ip -4 addr show docker0`.
# Jupiter's TTS_URL must be http://host.docker.internal:8004: the voice satellite treats that name as
# "not Helios" (so a sleeping Helios still gets woken).
#
# Install on Jupiter (one-time, as labadmin). Everything the server runs comes from the working Helios
# install, checked by sha256, plus the pinned package list tts/requirements-voxcpm.txt; nothing is piped
# from the internet into a shell. Keep /home/labadmin at mode 750: the service never needs to traverse
# it (systemd bind-mounts the four dirs below into an otherwise empty /home).
#   0. `nvidia-smi -L` lists both RTX 5080s. Note both UUIDs (GPU-xxxxxxxx-...) somewhere on Jupiter,
#      never in the repo or the PR: the higher-bus card is the voice (step 5), the other the experiment
#      pin. `nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps=gpu_bus_id,pid,process_name,used_memory --format=csv` shows
#      nothing on the voice card. Both cards need "Above 4G Decoding" on in the BIOS (with it off the
#      second card fails with "BAR1 is 0M" in dmesg and nvidia-smi lists one card).
#   1. Service user (no login, no home):  sudo useradd -r -M -s /usr/sbin/nologin voxcpm
#   2. Copy from Helios: the uv binary, uv's managed Python 3.11, the weights, and the voice config with
#      the one clip it uses (~4.9 GB, ~45 s on the LAN). Then the server and package list from git (the PR
#      branch until it is merged, then main). git show reads a ref without touching the live checkout:
#        ssh labadmin@10.0.0.195 'tar -C /home/labadmin -cf - .uv-pkg/bin/uv .local/share/uv/python models/VoxCPM2 tts-voices/voices.json tts-voices/jessica_sample.wav' \
#          | tar -C /home/labadmin -xf -
#        cd /home/labadmin/gateway_nerves && REF=origin/main && git fetch --no-write-fetch-head origin main
#        mkdir -p ~/voxcpm
#        git show $REF:tts/voxcpm_server.py > ~/voxcpm/voxcpm_server.py
#        git show $REF:tts/requirements-voxcpm.txt > ~/voxcpm/requirements-voxcpm.txt
#        git show $REF:tts/voxcpm-tts-jupiter.service > /tmp/voxcpm-tts-jupiter.service
#      then check the copies (must print OK three times):
#        cd ~ && printf '%s\n' \
#          'db919fb9428cc8ad04377ba3c898e0ec5fbee83700da5b982b1c9539f1e1b34f  .uv-pkg/bin/uv' \
#          'f7f964cfa9da23653baec6e6f7750719977ad944ed9f95fe52fe3a620506891d  models/VoxCPM2/model.safetensors' \
#          '94b5d51e107e0507d4acc976cfdadb64edd6fd06d1f751dadbf2fd1594274bf1  models/VoxCPM2/audiovae.pth' | sha256sum -c
#   3. Python env: uv-managed Python 3.11, which uv finds in ~/.local/share/uv/python from step 2. Not
#      the system Python: torch.compile needs Python.h. Exact versions come from Helios (~40 s):
#        cd ~/voxcpm && ~/.uv-pkg/bin/uv venv --python-preference only-managed --python 3.11 .venv
#        VIRTUAL_ENV=$PWD/.venv ~/.uv-pkg/bin/uv pip install --index-strategy unsafe-best-match \
#          --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128 -r requirements-voxcpm.txt
#   4. Let the service user read these files and nothing else. These are per-user ACLs, not
#      world-readable files:
#        setfacl -R -m u:voxcpm:rX,d:u:voxcpm:rX ~/voxcpm ~/tts-voices ~/.local/share/uv/python ~/models/VoxCPM2
#   5. Pick the card. CUDA takes a UUID, so the choice survives slot or PCI-order changes:
#        echo 'CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=GPU-<voice card UUID from step 0>' | sudo tee /etc/voxcpm-tts.env
#      and the same UUID in Jupiter's .env (JUPITER_TTS_GPU_UUID=GPU-...), then render + reload the
#      monitoring configs (scripts/generate-configs.sh, scripts/reload-monitoring.sh).
#   5b. The bearer key (readable by root and the service user only), and the same value in Jupiter's
#      .env as TTS_API_KEY (at cutover; `sudo cat /etc/voxcpm-tts/api-key`):
#        sudo install -d -m 750 -o root -g voxcpm /etc/voxcpm-tts
#        python3 -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))' | sudo install -m 640 -o root -g voxcpm /dev/stdin /etc/voxcpm-tts/api-key
#      A missing, unreadable or short key file fails the start (the server never runs open).
#   6. git show $REF:tts/voxcpm-tts-jupiter.socket > /tmp/voxcpm-tts-jupiter.socket
#      sudo cp /tmp/voxcpm-tts-jupiter.service /etc/systemd/system/voxcpm-tts.service
#      sudo cp /tmp/voxcpm-tts-jupiter.socket /etc/systemd/system/voxcpm-tts.socket
#      sudo systemctl daemon-reload && sudo systemctl enable --now voxcpm-tts.socket voxcpm-tts
#      The first start compiles kernels (torch.compile, a few minutes). They persist in
#      /var/cache/voxcpm, so later starts take ~15-30 s. Watch: journalctl -u voxcpm-tts -f
#      If it fails with "Permission denied" under /home/labadmin, re-run step 4.
#   7. Checks:
#      - The voxcpm python process (~7.4 GiB) is the only process on the voice card (query in step 0).
#      - From the orchestrator container (what Jess uses):
#          docker exec brain-orchestrator python -c "import urllib.request as u; print(u.urlopen('http://host.docker.internal:8004/health', timeout=5).read())"
#        returns healthy; the same for /voices answers 401 (no key).
#      - From any other LAN device (a laptop or Helios): curl -m 3 http://10.0.0.248:8004/health fails
#        (nothing listens there). `ss -ltn 'sport = :8004'` on Jupiter shows only 172.17.0.1:8004.
#      - `journalctl -u voxcpm-tts -u voxcpm-tts.socket | grep -i firewall` prints nothing (systemd
#        starts WITHOUT the IP filter, and says so there, if BPF firewalling is unavailable).
#        `systemctl show -p IPAddressAllow,IPAddressDeny voxcpm-tts.socket voxcpm-tts` shows the
#        Docker pools on the socket and deny-all on the service.
#      - Speed + memory comparison vs Helios: docs/VOICE_AND_TTS.md → VoxCPM2 on Jupiter, step 2.
#        Write down the used memory, and check its 7-day peak a week after cutover (query there).
#
# Weights: openbmb/VoxCPM2 (Apache-2.0), HF revision 32279effe8c19989596f05d353d1447f51d9e915, at
# /home/labadmin/models/VoxCPM2, loaded offline (sha256s in step 2).
# Logs: journalctl -u voxcpm-tts on Jupiter. Not in Loki or the self-audit: Jupiter's promtail ships
# Docker container logs only. Text is never logged.

[Unit]
Description=VoxCPM2 TTS Server for Brain Gateway (Jupiter)
# The listening socket comes from voxcpm-tts.socket (socket activation, see "Network").
Requires=voxcpm-tts.socket
After=voxcpm-tts.socket network-online.target nvidia-persistenced.service
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=simple
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=10
# Load ~15 s from a warm page cache; the first start also runs torch.compile.
TimeoutStartSec=600

# Card choice lives in /etc/voxcpm-tts.env (CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=GPU-<uuid>, step 5). No `-` prefix:
# a missing file must fail the start, not let CUDA pick whichever card comes first.
EnvironmentFile=/etc/voxcpm-tts.env
Environment="CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID"
Environment="HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1"
Environment="VOXCPM_MODEL=/home/labadmin/models/VoxCPM2"
Environment="VOXCPM_VOICES_DIR=/home/labadmin/tts-voices"
Environment="VOXCPM_PORT=8004"
# The listening socket is inherited from voxcpm-tts.socket (LISTEN_FDS); VOXCPM_HOST/PORT are unused.
Environment="VOXCPM_API_KEY_FILE=/etc/voxcpm-tts/api-key"
Environment="VOXCPM_OUTPUT_SR=24000"
# Writable state (torch.compile / triton kernels, any library home-dir cache) lives in
# /var/cache/voxcpm; everything under /home is a read-only bind.
CacheDirectory=voxcpm
Environment="HOME=/var/cache/voxcpm"
Environment="TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR=/var/cache/voxcpm/inductor"
Environment="TRITON_CACHE_DIR=/var/cache/voxcpm/triton"
Environment="XDG_CACHE_HOME=/var/cache/voxcpm"
# tqdm progress bars per synthesis turn the journal into "[blob data]".
Environment="TQDM_DISABLE=1"
# Peak RSS ~10.4 GiB during load + compile (Jupiter has 125 GiB, shared with all of production).
MemoryMax=16G

# Sandbox: as the Helios unit, with its own nologin user. ProtectHome=tmpfs hides the rest of /home,
# including the checkout and its .env (/home/labadmin/gateway_nerves).
User=voxcpm
Group=voxcpm
NoNewPrivileges=yes
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=tmpfs
BindReadOnlyPaths=/home/labadmin/voxcpm /home/labadmin/.local/share/uv/python /home/labadmin/tts-voices /home/labadmin/models/VoxCPM2
PrivateTmp=yes
ProtectProc=invisible
# Jupiter's data: Prometheus/Loki/Paperless/Immich mounts under /mnt, app data (Actual, Homepage)
# under /opt. ProtectSystem=strict only makes them read-only; hide them.
InaccessiblePaths=-/mnt -/media -/srv -/opt
DevicePolicy=closed
# CUDA opens every /dev/nvidiaN while enumerating, even with one card visible; without the node
# torch silently falls back to CPU. CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES (/etc/voxcpm-tts.env) limits it to the voice card.
DeviceAllow=/dev/nvidia0 rw
DeviceAllow=/dev/nvidia1 rw
DeviceAllow=/dev/nvidiactl rw
DeviceAllow=/dev/nvidia-uvm rw
DeviceAllow=/dev/nvidia-uvm-tools rw
ProtectKernelTunables=yes
ProtectKernelModules=yes
ProtectKernelLogs=yes
ProtectControlGroups=yes
ProtectClock=yes
ProtectHostname=yes
RestrictNamespaces=yes
RestrictRealtime=yes
RestrictSUIDSGID=yes
LockPersonality=yes
CapabilityBoundingSet=
AmbientCapabilities=
RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_INET AF_INET6 AF_UNIX
SystemCallArchitectures=native
UMask=0077
# Host-firewall substitute (ufw is inactive on Jupiter): no IP traffic at all for the server process.
# Inbound connections come through voxcpm-tts.socket, whose allow-list (Docker's pools) applies to the
# connections it accepts. NEVER add an IPAddressAllow here: it would also let the server connect out
# to every container. Do NOT add MemoryDenyWriteExecute or PrivateDevices: both break CUDA.
IPAddressDeny=any

WorkingDirectory=/home/labadmin/voxcpm
ExecStart=/home/labadmin/voxcpm/.venv/bin/python /home/labadmin/voxcpm/voxcpm_server.py

StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal
SyslogIdentifier=voxcpm-tts

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
